<title>GERMANY: France will cut deficit to 3.0 pct of GDP in 1997.</title>
<headline>France will cut deficit to 3.0 pct of GDP in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>KEMPTEN, Germany 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said on Tuesday that France would cut its deficit to four percent of gross domestic product in 1996 and three percent of GDP in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;France will make four percent in 1996 and three percent in 1997,&quot; he said at a press conference following a meeting of German and French finance ministry and central bank officials.</p>
</text>
